{
  "abstract": "Let r(P_s,t) denote the Ramsey number of the 3-uniform tight path with s edges versus a clique on t vertices. Results of Phelps and Rodl give r(P_2,t)=Theta(t^2/log t). In 2013, Cooper and Mubayi proved that r(P_s,t)=Theta(t^2) for every fixed s at least 4. For the remaining case s=3, they asked for the order of r(P_3,t), a question later reiterated by Bohman, Mubayi and Picollelli. Together, these results give a lower bound of Omega(t^2/log t) and an upper bound of O(t^2) for r(P_3,t). We improve the upper bound to O(t^2/log log t), making progress towards a conjecture of Mattheus, Mubayi, Nie and Verstraete. The main upper bound is formalized unconditionally in Lean 4.",
  "authors": [
    {
      "name": "Abhishek Methuku"
    }
